 " of the Soviet Union, the 1987 World runner-up, " [:a {:href "/athletes/60680"} "Dennis Koslowski"] " of the United States, the 1986 World Champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/58571"} "Tamás Gáspár"] " of Hungary, the 1986 European Champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/60892"} "Jožef Tertei"] " of Yugoslavia, and the 1987 European Champion, " [:a {:href "/athletes/57395"} "Iliya Georgiev"] " of Bulgaria. None of them made the final match but Wroński did, although he lost in Group A to Gedakhauri in round three. Koslowski and Tertei also had one loss in Group A, but Wroński had defeated them both head-to-head, which was the deciding factor. In the final Wroński met West German " [:a {:href "/athletes/58370"} "Gerhard Himmel"] ", who went undefeated in Group B. The final was close but Wroński prevailed on decision, 3-1, to win a surprising gold medal. Koslowski took bronze by defeating Georgiev, 6-0. Koslowski would improve at Barcelona in four years and win a silver medal, while Wroński placed fourth, but Wroński would win a second gold medal in this class at Atlanta in 1996."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "17"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59702"} "Andrzej Wroński"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "10"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/58370"} "Gerhard Himmel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; v